name    mod-procedural-dungeon: a death on map 760 (zone 5100) ends alive at the entrance, never at a graveyard
# Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1. Zone 5100 has no graveyard_zone row; the core's fallback for a
# release there is Westfall. The interim (operator 2026-10-16: "sollen vorerst einfach am anfang respawnen"): the
# module resurrects a dead player on its next 1 Hz tick at the entrance (or the last cleared boss hall), and no
# release on map 760 reaches the core's graveyard search. A fresh layout has no cleared boss hall, so the
# director must come back where it entered.
# The director generates a layout for its account and enters with `enter force` (no FLStream.dll on a bot
# session - the server side builds the map all the same). It dies and releases at once: the release is held
# back, and the tick brings it back alive and unsickened at the entrance on map 760.
timeout 120s

bot a warrior
group none

place 727 13288.5 11776.2 -31.5
as gm .pdungeon v2 gen
expect output has "pdungeon v2: seed"
as gm .pdungeon v2 enter force
waitfor gm map 760 timeout 20s
wait 3s
mark start

log 1 - die and release at once
do gm die
expect gm dead
do gm release
expect gm map 760
waitfor gm alive timeout 5s
expect gm map 760
expect gm at start 15
expect gm noaura 15007

log 2 - a second death in the same run, no release
do gm die
waitfor gm alive timeout 5s
expect gm map 760
expect gm at start 15

cleanup
place 727 13288.5 11776.2 -31.5
